arch=arm64
vmlinux_btf=6.6 kernel BTF dump (bpftool btf dump file /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux format c)
clang=Ubuntu clang version 18.1.3 (1ubuntu1)
load_verified=x86 only: bpftool prog loadall, CentOS Stream 8 (4.18.0-326.el8)
notes=clang was not captured when these objects were committed; the value above
  was recovered afterwards from the object's own DWARF producer string
  (readelf -p .debug_str), so it is what built THIS file rather than a note
  taken by hand. The vmlinux_btf line is still only a description -- the exact
  dump is not kept, so a byte-identical rebuild cannot be reproduced from this
  repository alone. See prebuilt/README.md. A rebuild with a different clang can
  change which helpers are outlined, which is what tools/check_bpf_symbols.sh
  asserts against.
